    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="50.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 50.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="50.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="346" ed="#liebermann"/>[Y]fel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.10"/> æwbryce byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.11-2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> eawfæst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.12-2"/> man mid æmtige forlicge, ⁊ mycele wyrse wið oðres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.13"/> æwe oððe wið gehadode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.14"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="50.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="346" ed="#liebermann"/>Yfel æwbryce bið, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> eawfeste men<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.3"/> wið emtige [hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.1"/>] forlicge, ⁊ mycele wyrse wið oðres æwe oððe wið gehadode.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="50.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="346" ed="#liebermann"/>Yfel æwbryce bið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> æwfæst mann wið emtige forlicge, ⁊ micele wyrse wyð oðres æwe oððe wið gehadod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="50.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="347" ed="#liebermann"/>Malum adulterium est, si sponsus cum uacua<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.11"/> fornicetur, et multo peius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.12"/> cum sponsa alterius uel cum ordinata.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="50.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="347" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.15"/> coniugium quis uiolauerit, uidelicet iacendo sub coniuge sua, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.16"/> fornicatus fuerit cum alia femina uel, quod peius est, cum alterius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.17"/> coniugata, faciat pęnitentiam secundum librum pęnitentialem.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.18"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="50.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="347" ed="#liebermann"/>[50, 1] Mala quidem legalis instituti transgressio est, ut quis cum uacua concumbat, peior uero cum desponsata uel cum sacrata.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="50.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="200" ed="#robertson"/>Yfel æwbryce bið þæt eawfeste m[a]n<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_50-1.robnote.fn.8"/> wið emtige [hine]<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_50-1.robnote.fn.9"/> forlicge, ⁊ mycele wyrse wið oðres æwe oððe wið gehadode.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="282" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Yfel æwbryce byð þæt eawfæst man mid æmtige forlicge, and mycele wyrse wið oðres æwe oððe wið gehadode.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="347" ed="#liebermann"/>Schlimmer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.de.1"/> Ehebruch ist es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.de.2"/>, dass ein verehelichter Mann mit einer Ledigen hurt, und viel schlimmer mit der Ehefrau eines anderen oder mit einer [Gott<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_50-1.lnote.de.3"/>] Geweihten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It is a bad adultery when a married man fornicates with an unmarried woman, and much worse with another man's wife or with a woman consecrated [to God].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="201" ed="#robertson"/>It is wicked adultery for a pious man to commit fornication with an unmarried woman, and much worse [for him to do so] with the wife of another man or with any woman who has taken religious vows.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="470" ed="#whitelock"/>It is wicked adultery that a married man should commit fornication with a single woman, and much worse if with another’s wife or with a woman consecrated [to God].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="283" ed="#rabin-doml"/>It is a terrible transgression for a married man to have intercourse with an unmarried woman, and much worse with another’s wife or with a woman in orders.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">In G, ‘[Y]fel’ has space for a coloured initial.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 347, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Yfel: fel with space for the initial in G</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">man: men B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> man</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read man</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">muliere <hi rend="italic">fügt zu K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">muliere added by K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si added by Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fel, <hi rend="italic">davor Raum für</hi> [<hi rend="italic">farbige</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Initiale G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fel, preceded by a space for a [coloured] initial G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.12-2" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so G B;</hi> æwf. man wiþ ænige hine f. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus G B; æwf. man wiþ ænige hine f. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oþers <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oþers Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dod <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dod Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">bid <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">bid A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Qui c. uiol. <hi rend="italic">H Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Qui c. uiol. H Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so S; fehlt H Di Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus S; lacking in H Di Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">alia <hi rend="italic">Lb;</hi> aliqua <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">alia Lb; aliqua S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">51 <hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">51 lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 50³; zum Stile 46, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 50³; on the style 46, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 50³; zum Stile 46, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 50³; on the style 46, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_50-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Nonne 13b; Mönchin und zur Keuschheit Eingesegnete ist gemeint; <hi rend="italic">ebd</hi>. 1. Cnut befiehlt deren Keuschheit auch I 6a. 7, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Nonne 13b; a nun and a woman consecrated to chastity are meant; <hi rend="italic">ibid</hi>. 1. Cnut also commands their chastity in I 6a. 7, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_50-1.robnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope></bibl><label>m[a]n</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">G, A, Ld; <hi rend="italic">men</hi> B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_50-1.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope></bibl><label>hine</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A, Ld; written above the line in 16th cent. in B.</seg></note>
